      "side": 1,
      "message": "I had look at the Consul code and it doesn\u0027t seem to me that node name is consul agent. You can however set the \u0027near\u0027 parameter to \u0027_agent\u0027 and then it would sort the list of services in the ascending order RTT from the consul agent node. \nYou may refer the Consul code https://github.com/hashicorp/consul/blob/3b3cb0d07b6e045359394b639e765a595f5c1668/consul/catalog_endpoint.go; Function of interest is below  \u003d\u003e \nfunc (c *Catalog) ServiceNodes(args *structs.ServiceSpecificRequest, reply *structs.IndexedServiceNodes).",
